You are implementing a Blazor Web App for a logistics company that tracks shipments. The project is already scaffolded at `/tmp/sv-f80d141473b64d2f80db8e00c3605495/ShipmentTracker/` with:
- **InteractiveAuto, Global** render mode
- **Individual authentication** (ASP.NET Core Identity with SQLite)
- Two projects: `ShipmentTracker` (server) and `ShipmentTracker.Client` (WebAssembly)

## Architecture Rules (Auto mode)
- All interactive components MUST go in the `.Client` project (`ShipmentTracker.Client/Pages/`)
- Interactive components CANNOT access DbContext directly — they must use HTTP APIs
- Define service interfaces in `.Client`, implement with HttpClient in `.Client`, implement with direct DB access in server
- Register matching services in both `Program.cs` files
- Identity/Account pages in server project must stay static SSR — do NOT touch them

## What to implement

### 1. Data Model — Server project (`ShipmentTracker/Data/`)

Create `Shipment.cs` model:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Data;

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Cancelled
}

public class Shipment
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

Add `DbSet<Shipment>` to `ApplicationDbContext`. Create and apply a migration.

### 2. Shared DTO — Client project (`ShipmentTracker.Client/`)

Create `ShipmentDto.cs` in the Client project root (since both projects reference it):
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client;

public enum ShipmentStatus
{
    Pending,
    PickedUp,
    InTransit,
    OutForDelivery,
    Delivered,
    Cancelled
}

public class ShipmentDto
{
    public int Id { get; set; }
    public string TrackingNumber { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Origin { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Destination { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public ShipmentStatus Status { get; set; }
    public DateTime CreatedAt { get; set; }
    public DateTime? EstimatedDelivery { get; set; }
    public DateTime? ActualDelivery { get; set; }
    public string CustomerEmail { get; set; } = string.Empty;
    public string Description { get; set; } = string.Empty;
}
```

### 3. Service Interface — Client project

Create `IShipmentService.cs` in Client project root:
```csharp
namespace ShipmentTracker.Client;

public interface IShipmentService
{
    Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync();
    Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber);
    Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(ShipmentDto shipment);
    Task<ShipmentDto> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status);
}
```

### 4. Client-side implementation — Client project

Create `ShipmentHttpService.cs`:
```csharp
using System.Net.Http.Json;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Client;

public class ShipmentHttpService(HttpClient http) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
        => await http.GetFromJsonAsync<List<ShipmentDto>>("api/shipments") ?? [];

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var response = await http.GetAsync($"api/shipments/track/{Uri.EscapeDataString(trackingNumber)}");
        if (!response.IsSuccessStatusCode) return null;
        return await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>();
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(ShipmentDto shipment)
    {
        var response = await http.PostAsJsonAsync("api/shipments", shipment);
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>())!;
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus status)
    {
        var response = await http.PutAsJsonAsync($"api/shipments/{id}/status", new { Status = status });
        response.EnsureSuccessStatusCode();
        return (await response.Content.ReadFromJsonAsync<ShipmentDto>())!;
    }
}
```

### 5. Server-side implementation — Server project

Create `ShipmentServerService.cs` in `ShipmentTracker/Services/`:
```csharp
using Microsoft.EntityFrameworkCore;
using ShipmentTracker.Client;
using ShipmentTracker.Data;

namespace ShipmentTracker.Services;

public class ShipmentServerService(ApplicationDbContext db) : IShipmentService
{
    public async Task<List<ShipmentDto>> GetAllShipmentsAsync()
        => await db.Shipments.OrderByDescending(s => s.CreatedAt).Select(s => MapToDto(s)).ToListAsync();

    public async Task<ShipmentDto?> GetShipmentByTrackingNumberAsync(string trackingNumber)
    {
        var shipment = await db.Shipments.FirstOrDefaultAsync(s => s.TrackingNumber == trackingNumber);
        return shipment is null ? null : MapToDto(shipment);
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto> CreateShipmentAsync(ShipmentDto dto)
    {
        var shipment = new Shipment
        {
            TrackingNumber = $"ST-{DateTime.UtcNow:yyyyMMdd}-{Random.Shared.Next(1000, 9999)}",
            Origin = dto.Origin,
            Destination = dto.Destination,
            Status = Data.ShipmentStatus.Pending,
            CreatedAt = DateTime.UtcNow,
            EstimatedDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow.AddDays(7),
            CustomerEmail = dto.CustomerEmail,
            Description = dto.Description
        };
        db.Shipments.Add(shipment);
        await db.SaveChangesAsync();
        return MapToDto(shipment);
    }

    public async Task<ShipmentDto> UpdateShipmentStatusAsync(int id, ShipmentStatus newStatus)
    {
        var shipment = await db.Shipments.FindAsync(id) ?? throw new KeyNotFoundException($"Shipment {id} not found");
        shipment.Status = (Data.ShipmentStatus)(int)newStatus;
        if (newStatus == ShipmentStatus.Delivered)
            shipment.ActualDelivery = DateTime.UtcNow;
        await db.SaveChangesAsync();
        return MapToDto(shipment);
    }

    private static ShipmentDto MapToDto(Shipment s) => new()
    {
        Id = s.Id,
        TrackingNumber = s.TrackingNumber,
        Origin = s.Origin,
        Destination = s.Destination,
        Status = (ShipmentStatus)(int)s.Status,
        CreatedAt = s.CreatedAt,
        EstimatedDelivery = s.EstimatedDelivery,
        ActualDelivery = s.ActualDelivery,
        CustomerEmail = s.CustomerEmail,
        Description = s.Description
    };
}
```

### 6. API Endpoints — Server `Program.cs`

Add minimal API endpoints in `Program.cs` BEFORE `app.Run()`. All endpoints should require authorization. Add these:

```csharp
// Shipment API endpoints
